We are continuing the existing game exactly as it has been designed and built so far. Do NOT rebuild unrelated pages, do NOT invent replacement systems, and do NOT remove existing functionality unless explicitly instructed below.

IMPORTANT OVERALL DIRECTION:
We are now simplifying the free version and aligning the lesson progression with the boss/tower progression.

FREE VERSION:
- The free version should contain 15 lessons.
- The free version should contain the first 5 bosses.
- The relationship should be structurally aligned:
  5 bosses × 3 lessons per boss = 15 lessons.
- The paid/full version should contain the full 30-lesson progression and the full tower/boss progression.
- Do NOT remove or renumber the existing bosses to make this work.
- Do NOT change the lore, boss identities, or existing story structure.
- We are choosing this 15-free-lessons / 5-free-bosses approach intentionally because it is much cleaner than trying to redistribute 30 lessons across only 5 free bosses.
- Future major updates can expand the game with additional lessons, bosses, gameplay, and lore.

LESSON PROGRESSION:
The progression should feel like:

Lesson → Minion → Lesson → Minion → Lesson → Minion → Boss

Then the next boss section continues with the next set of lessons/minions.

For the free version:
- Boss 1 has its corresponding 3-lesson progression and its 3 regular enemies/minions.
- Boss 2 has the next 3 lessons and its 3 regular enemies/minions.
- Boss 3 has the next 3 lessons and its 3 regular enemies/minions.
- Boss 4 has the next 3 lessons and its 3 regular enemies/minions.
- Boss 5 has the final 3 lessons and its 3 regular enemies/minions.
- The exact existing minion/boss identities and existing game data should be preserved.
- Do not invent new lessons just to fill gaps if the existing GitHub lesson data already contains the required content.
- Make sure the actual lesson content from the repository is active rather than placeholder/title-only lessons.
- There must be exactly 15 lessons available in the free version.
- The full version should contain exactly 30 lessons.
- If the repository currently contains extra lesson slots/data beyond the intended 30, do not expose them in the game. Do not invent content for them.

LESSON PROGRESSION UI:
On the Home page, keep the existing Tower progression component.

Add an equivalent progression component for lessons:
- Arabic title: "دروسك" (Your Lessons).
- It should visually match the existing "برجك" / Your Tower progression.
- Instead of 10 separated progression segments, the lesson progression should contain 30 separated segments in the full version.
- In the free version, the first 15 segments are available and the remaining 15 should clearly communicate that they belong to the full version/locked progression.
- The segments must be visually separated in the same way as the Tower progression.
- Progress should be visually reflected by changing the segment state/color as the player advances.
- Preserve the game's existing visual language rather than creating a completely different component.

When the player clicks/taps the lesson progression component:
- Open the complete lesson progression/list.
- Show which lessons have been completed.
- Show the current lesson.
- Show which lessons are still locked/not completed.
- Make the progression understandable at a glance.
- The player should not be forced to blindly progress through Lesson 1 → Lesson 2 → Lesson 3 without ever being able to see their overall lesson progression.
- The lesson progression should work similarly in concept to the existing Tower progression.

CONTINUE YOUR JOURNEY:
The Home page's "Continue Your Journey" button should remain the main entry point for the player's current progression.

When the player presses Continue Your Journey:
1. Take them directly to their current lesson.
2. For a new player, this means Lesson 1.
3. After completing the lesson, DO NOT simply send the player automatically to the next lesson.
4. Instead, the next step should be the appropriate gameplay/minion encounter connected to that lesson progression.
5. The player should be able to enter the appropriate regular enemy/minion encounter before progressing onward to the next lesson.
6. The progression should therefore feel like learning → applying what was learned → progressing through the tower.

GAMEPLAY MODES:
VERY IMPORTANT:
We are NOT inventing new gameplay modes.

Use the SAME gameplay modes that were already built in the previous version of the game, with the SAME existing names and implementations.

There are FOUR gameplay modes:
1. The existing multiple-choice mode.
2. The existing mode where the player combines words to create a sentence.
3. The existing mode where the player combines letters to create a word.
4. The existing Tetris-like gameplay mode.

Use the exact existing names that are already present in the project. Do not rename them, replace them, or create alternative versions.

IMPORTANT LOCATION OF THESE MODES:
These gameplay modes should NOT be displayed as four large options on the Home page.

The Home page should remain focused on progression and important information.

Instead:
- Player presses Continue Your Journey.
- Player completes the relevant lesson.
- Player reaches the relevant minion/regular enemy encounter.
- At that encounter, provide access to the FOUR existing gameplay modes.
- The player chooses which mode to use for that encounter.
- The same structure should work for the first, second, and third minion of the boss section.
- Then the player proceeds to the boss after completing the required minion progression.

FREE VS PAID GAMEPLAY:
The first three gameplay modes are available in the free version.

The fourth mode — the existing Tetris-like mode — is a FULL/PREMIUM feature.

Therefore:
- Show all four gameplay modes at the appropriate minion/gameplay selection screen.
- Do NOT hide the Tetris-like mode completely.
- The Tetris-like mode should visibly exist but be locked/greyed out for free users.
- When a free user attempts to access it, show an appropriate premium/full-version message.
- This is intentional: the player should be able to see what they would unlock by upgrading.
- Do not put this Tetris-like mode on the Home page merely to advertise it. Its natural location is inside the actual gameplay/minion flow.

MINIONS:
The first boss has three regular enemies/minions before the boss.
They are NOT minibosses; treat them as regular enemies/minions.

The first minion should be greyed/locked if the player has not reached it yet.
Do NOT show the first three minions as already completed/green for a brand-new player.

A new player opening the game for the first time must see:
- First minion = available/current when the progression reaches it.
- Later minions = locked/not yet completed.
- Boss = locked until its required progression is completed.

Do not use saved/test/demo state that makes the first three minions appear completed for a fresh account/session.

After completing the relevant lesson:
- Take the player to the correct minion.
- Allow them to choose among the four existing gameplay modes.
- After completing the minion, continue to the next required progression step.
- Repeat for the second and third minions.
- Then unlock/enable the corresponding boss encounter.

DO NOT REDIRECT TO THE OLD SECOND TAB:
The current implementation has been incorrectly redirecting the player to the old second tab containing the Tower/map interface.

That is NOT the correct destination for the gameplay flow.

Do not use the old second tab as the gameplay destination.

The second tab/page will later be redesigned for Online and Co-op functionality. That is a separate task and is NOT part of this prompt.

For this prompt, focus only on making the lesson → minion → gameplay-mode → boss progression actually work.

HOME PAGE:
Keep the improvements already made:
- Settings/gear icon remains correctly positioned in the upper-left corner.
- Do not move it downward again.
- If necessary, lower the other upper-page elements — Champion title, Level, Tower area, XP gauge, XP counter, XP label, etc. — to create enough visual space so the Settings icon can remain properly positioned in the true upper-left corner.
- The Settings icon should have its own space and should not be forced lower because other UI elements occupy the top area.

Keep:
- XP/progression display.
- Coins.
- League.
- Streak.
- Tower progression.
- Word of the Day.
- Lucky Wheel.
- Continue Your Journey.
- RoboSpecter tips.

RoboSpecter should be positioned ABOVE Continue Your Journey if that fits the existing layout cleanly, because important guidance should be visible before the player reaches the bottom of the page.

LUCKY WHEEL:
The Lucky Wheel animation is now working on both phone and PC/browser.
Do NOT break it.
Keep the spinning animation.
Do not replace it with a static reward appearing immediately.

WORD OF THE DAY:
Keep it functional and available as it currently works.
Do not unnecessarily lock it behind defeating bosses if the current intended design is that it is available to the player.

FULL TRIAL / SUBSCRIPTION:
Keep the Full Trial/premium functionality that was recently restored.

There must also be a clear way for a free user to upgrade/subscribe to the full version.
The subscription/full-version entry should exist on the Home page, preferably toward the bottom where it does not clutter the main progression UI.

Do not remove the upgrade path.

TUTORIAL:
The current tutorial is substantially better, but simplify it.

The tutorial should primarily teach the player how to start playing:
- Explain the Continue button.
- Highlight the Continue button.
- Make the highlighted target visually illuminated/brighter while the rest of the interface is dimmed.
- A golden border/frame alone is NOT enough.
- The actual target should visually stand out/light up.
- The player should clearly understand: "Press this to continue your current lesson."

Do NOT make the tutorial unnecessarily explain every tab on the Home page.

Remove unnecessary tutorial steps such as:
- Explaining the Tower tab while the player is already being guided into their lesson.
- Highlighting the second tab during the lesson-start tutorial.
- Jumping between Item Shop → Leaderboard → Achievements → Lucky Wheel in an unnecessarily long sequence.

The tutorial should be focused, coherent, and sequential.

Do not make the tutorial feel like a tour of every button in the application.

ARABIC TEXT / HARAKAT:
IMPORTANT QUALITY CONTROL:
Review the Arabic lesson content carefully.

The existing lessons contain Arabic diacritic/harakat mistakes.

Specifically check:
- Fatha.
- Damma.
- Kasra.
- Sukun.
- Shadda.
- Tanween.
- Other Arabic harakat/diacritics used throughout the lessons.

For example, in the word for "hello" (مرحبًا), the tanween should be correctly placed according to proper Arabic orthography, not incorrectly placed on the wrong letter.

Likewise, in "thank you, friend" / the relevant Arabic phrase, make sure the tanween and other harakat are attached to the correct letters.

Do NOT treat these as isolated mistakes.
Audit the lesson content for the same type of Arabic harakat/diacritic errors throughout the lessons.

Preserve correct Arabic spelling and grammar.
Do not randomly add or remove harakat.
Use proper Arabic orthography.

LESSON DATA:
The repository/GitHub already contains lesson data/content.

Do not leave lessons after Lesson 5 as title-only placeholders if actual lesson content exists in the repository.

Activate the actual existing lesson content.

There must be:
- 15 usable lessons in the free version.
- 30 usable lessons in the full version.

Do not expose placeholder lessons as if they were real lessons.

Do not silently invent lesson content.
Do not silently delete real lesson content.
If there is a discrepancy in the repository's lesson count, prioritize the intended product structure above and keep the exposed product progression at exactly 15 free / 30 full.

IMPORTANT IMPLEMENTATION RULE:
Before changing the lesson/boss progression, inspect the existing project structure and existing game-mode implementations.

Reuse existing components, data, names, routes, and gameplay implementations wherever possible.

Do not rebuild something that already exists.

Do not create fake placeholder routes just to make navigation appear to work.

The final flow must be genuinely connected:
Home → Continue Your Journey → Lesson → Correct Minion → Four Gameplay Mode Selection → Selected Existing Gameplay Mode → Next Minion → Boss → Next Lesson/Progression.

Do not send the player to a dead-end page.

Do not send the player to the old Tower/map tab as a substitute for the actual gameplay encounter.

TEST THIS FLOW:
Test it as a completely new/free player.

Verify:
1. Home page loads correctly.
2. Tutorial starts correctly and highlights the Continue button with an actual illuminated/highlighted target.
3. Continue Your Journey opens Lesson 1.
4. Completing Lesson 1 does NOT open Lesson 2 immediately.
5. Completing Lesson 1 sends the player to the correct first minion/gameplay encounter.
6. The first minion is not falsely marked as completed.
7. The four existing gameplay modes are visible at the appropriate gameplay-selection point.
8. The first three modes work for free users.
9. The fourth Tetris-like mode is visible but locked for free users and correctly communicates the premium requirement.
10. Completing the first minion leads correctly to the next progression step.
11. The three minions and boss progression works in the correct order.
12. The next lesson becomes available at the correct point.
13. The lesson progression component updates correctly.
14. Clicking the lesson progression opens the complete lesson list/progression.
15. The free user sees exactly 15 available lessons.
16. The full user sees exactly 30 lessons.
17. No placeholder lessons are incorrectly presented as completed/active content.
18. Arabic harakat/diacritics are correctly rendered throughout the lesson content.
19. The Lucky Wheel animation still works on PC and mobile.
20. The Full Trial/upgrade path still works.
21. No changes are made to the future Online/Co-op second-tab redesign in this task.

DO NOT OVER-REFACTOR:
This prompt is specifically about:
- Home-page progression.
- Lesson progression.
- Lesson list/progression UI.
- Lesson → minion → gameplay → boss flow.
- Existing gameplay-mode access.
- Free/premium gameplay distinction.
- Tutorial cleanup.
- Arabic harakat quality.
- Correct navigation.

Do not redesign the Store, Achievements, Leaderboards, Online, Co-op, or other secondary pages in this task.

Those will be handled separately, page by page.

Most importantly: do not just make the UI LOOK like the flow works. Make the underlying navigation and progression actually work using the existing game systems.
